From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 016/NNN] upper: test for __GLIBC_PREREQ before calling it

__GLIBC_PREREQ exists only on glibc. Using it unguarded makes ipv6.h a
preprocessor error on musl and on Darwin, because an undefined function-like
macro in a #if is a parse error rather than a false.

Nesting the check is the only form that works: putting it behind a
defined() test in the same expression does not help, since the preprocessor
still has to parse the call.

--- a/lib/include/srsran/upper/ipv6.h	2026-09-03 15:45:40
+++ b/lib/include/srsran/upper/ipv6.h	2026-09-03 15:46:28
@@ -25,7 +25,18 @@
 #include <linux/in6.h>
 
 // as of glibc 2.19, the IPv6 issue seems to be fixed https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=15850
+// __GLIBC_PREREQ only exists on glibc. Testing it inside a larger expression
+// does not help, because the preprocessor still has to parse the call, so the
+// check has to be nested.
+#if defined(__GLIBC_PREREQ)
 #if __GLIBC_PREREQ(2, 19)
+#define SRSRAN_HAVE_LINUX_IPV6_H 1
+#endif
+#else
+#define SRSRAN_HAVE_LINUX_IPV6_H 1
+#endif
+
+#ifdef SRSRAN_HAVE_LINUX_IPV6_H
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
 #else
 // Some versions of glibc yield to a compile error with gcc
